WEBVTT

00:00:00.332 --> 00:00:02.724
Grid Bot Builder. Grid Bot Blueprint.

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:07.406
Lesson one. Introduction. Education only.

00:00:07.905 --> 00:00:10.667
Not financial advice. This is general

00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:13.174
information and doesn't consider your

00:00:13.174 --> 00:00:15.834
objectives, financial situation or needs.

00:00:16.294 --> 00:00:18.989
Crypto is high risk. You could lose all

00:00:18.989 --> 00:00:22.008
the money you put in. Crypto carries a

00:00:22.008 --> 00:00:25.594
risk of total loss. The prices are public

00:00:25.594 --> 00:00:28.091
historical daily closes, marked Example.

00:00:29.261 --> 00:00:31.326
Past performance is not a reliable

00:00:31.326 --> 00:00:34.836
indicator of future results. A grid bot

00:00:34.836 --> 00:00:37.516
places waiting buy orders on lines below

00:00:37.516 --> 00:00:40.118
the price and sell orders on lines above

00:00:40.118 --> 00:00:42.561
it, inside a top and a bottom you choose.

00:00:43.021 --> 00:00:45.734
The space between your top and your bottom

00:00:45.734 --> 00:00:48.254
is called the band. A limit order is an

00:00:48.254 --> 00:00:51.051
order that waits at a price you choose. It

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:54.537
does not chase the price. The sells above

00:00:54.537 --> 00:00:57.039
need some coin, so a grid starts with part

00:00:57.039 --> 00:00:59.754
cash and part coin. Cash is money you can

00:00:59.754 --> 00:01:02.632
spend. Coin is the crypto. That is a

00:01:02.632 --> 00:01:04.761
description, not advice about what to

00:01:04.761 --> 00:01:07.914
hold. A stop is a rule you write down

00:01:07.914 --> 00:01:10.263
before you start, saying what you will do

00:01:10.263 --> 00:01:12.611
if the price leaves the band and does not

00:01:12.611 --> 00:01:16.197
come back. When a chart says Example, it

00:01:16.197 --> 00:01:18.363
means a real past price used as an

00:01:18.363 --> 00:01:21.818
example, not a forecast. By the end you

00:01:21.818 --> 00:01:25.511
will know what a grid bot places. You will

00:01:25.511 --> 00:01:28.837
see that idea on one real path from 2023.

00:01:30.007 --> 00:01:32.560
You will be able to say the stop rule in

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:35.176
one sentence. Think of a ladder leaned on

00:01:35.176 --> 00:01:37.505
a wall. The rungs wait, and they do not

00:01:37.505 --> 00:01:40.308
chase you. The ladder is the analogy, and

00:01:40.308 --> 00:01:42.806
the chart beside it is the real past path.

00:01:43.826 --> 00:01:46.088
The range is the top line and the bottom

00:01:46.088 --> 00:01:48.763
line, copied from the path. Every close in

00:01:48.763 --> 00:01:50.763
this window stayed between those two

00:01:50.648 --> 00:01:53.080
lines. A neat round box would have sat

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:55.138
inside the real lines, so it does not

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:58.214
match the path. The range is a top and a

00:01:58.214 --> 00:02:01.205
bottom you draw before any rung. Without a

00:02:01.205 --> 00:02:03.263
top and a bottom, you can't place the

00:02:03.154 --> 00:02:06.984
lines. Seven price lines sit between that

00:02:06.984 --> 00:02:09.309
bottom and that top, with six gaps of

00:02:09.309 --> 00:02:12.398
about 900 dollars between them. The screen

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:14.947
shows each price. A limit order waits on a

00:02:14.947 --> 00:02:17.395
level. It does not run after the price.

00:02:18.415 --> 00:02:20.639
The levels are limit orders that wait on

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:23.124
the rungs. A limit order sits at a price.

00:02:23.584 --> 00:02:27.064
It does not chase. A fence has a top rail

00:02:27.064 --> 00:02:29.876
and a bottom rail. Inside them, the price

00:02:29.876 --> 00:02:32.599
can wander. On the chart those rails are

00:02:32.599 --> 00:02:35.643
the bottom line and the top line. The

00:02:35.643 --> 00:02:37.921
daily close is the last price of the day.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:40.686
Crypto trades all day, so the day is cut

00:02:40.686 --> 00:02:45.038
at a set time. This candle is 19 July

00:02:45.038 --> 00:02:47.393
2023. The high, the low, and the close are

00:02:47.393 --> 00:02:50.148
labelled. A wick is the thin line from the

00:02:50.148 --> 00:02:52.660
close out to the high or the low. It is

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:56.152
not the close. The example is Bitcoin's

00:02:56.152 --> 00:02:59.509
public daily price in US dollars. From 19

00:02:59.509 --> 00:03:03.732
July 2023 to 16 October 2023, every one of

00:03:03.732 --> 00:03:08.030
those days closed inside the band. We do

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:10.475
not need to read each day. The shape is

00:03:10.475 --> 00:03:13.616
the lesson, and it is marked Example. A

00:03:13.616 --> 00:03:15.893
stop is a rule you write down before you

00:03:15.893 --> 00:03:17.958
start, saying what you will do if the

00:03:17.958 --> 00:03:20.235
price leaves the band and does not come

00:03:20.235 --> 00:03:23.408
back. On 23 October 2023 the close

00:03:23.408 --> 00:03:27.000
finished above the top line. The price did

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.889
not come back, so this example was

00:03:28.726 --> 00:03:31.894
finished. Write your stop rule down before

00:03:31.894 --> 00:03:34.530
you start. On the card it says: Stop =

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:39.644
when you quit. Worked check for 19 July

00:03:39.644 --> 00:03:44.030
2023 to 16 October 2023. The bottom line

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:46.400
and the top line are on the card, with

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:49.535
seven lines and six gaps of about 900. The

00:03:49.535 --> 00:03:51.839
stop rule is: if the daily close leaves

00:03:51.839 --> 00:03:54.143
the top line and does not come back, the

00:03:54.143 --> 00:03:56.910
idea is finished. Nothing in that list is

00:03:56.910 --> 00:04:00.007
an order. Price often moves sideways,

00:04:00.007 --> 00:04:02.388
bouncing between the same top and bottom

00:04:02.388 --> 00:04:05.114
instead of leaving. A grid is a ladder of

00:04:05.114 --> 00:04:07.548
limit orders built for that bouncing, and

00:04:07.548 --> 00:04:09.911
it has nothing to do while price runs one

00:04:09.911 --> 00:04:13.174
way and stays there. A grid has three

00:04:13.174 --> 00:04:15.509
parts you can name: the range, the levels,

00:04:15.506 --> 00:04:18.568
and the stop. The range is the band. The

00:04:18.568 --> 00:04:22.028
levels are the rungs inside it. Buy orders

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:24.292
sit on lines below the price and sell

00:04:24.292 --> 00:04:27.082
orders sit on lines above it. The sells

00:04:27.082 --> 00:04:29.538
need some coin, so a grid starts with part

00:04:29.538 --> 00:04:32.405
cash and part coin. That is a description,

00:04:32.405 --> 00:04:35.540
not advice. No order is sent from this

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:38.562
lesson. You draw the idea. If a screen

00:04:38.562 --> 00:04:41.057
appears later, it should be a copy of the

00:04:41.057 --> 00:04:44.296
page, and only on paper or demo. The

00:04:44.296 --> 00:04:46.574
course is a map, and this introduction is

00:04:46.475 --> 00:04:48.685
only the first square. Next is a

00:04:48.685 --> 00:04:51.089
checklist, then the definition, then

00:04:51.089 --> 00:04:53.494
regimes, then spacing and range, then

00:04:53.494 --> 00:04:56.058
entry and exit, then a paper screen, then

00:04:56.058 --> 00:04:58.703
monitoring, then mistakes, then scaling,

00:04:58.703 --> 00:05:02.485
then an opt-in lesson on liquidation. Draw

00:05:02.485 --> 00:05:04.819
a path that leaves the top of the band and

00:05:04.779 --> 00:05:07.435
does not return. The rungs below are still

00:05:07.435 --> 00:05:09.602
there, but the bouncing they were built

00:05:09.405 --> 00:05:11.923
for is gone. Leave through the top and

00:05:11.923 --> 00:05:14.288
every sell has filled, so you hold mostly

00:05:14.288 --> 00:05:16.509
cash, and leave through the bottom and

00:05:16.509 --> 00:05:18.802
every buy has filled, so you hold mostly

00:05:18.802 --> 00:05:21.819
coin. There is no result number in this

00:05:21.819 --> 00:05:24.323
lesson. A result number would pretend the

00:05:24.323 --> 00:05:27.864
example already happened. The example is a

00:05:27.877 --> 00:05:30.664
drawing of a mechanism. The next step is

00:05:30.664 --> 00:05:33.046
the setup checklist, on paper, before any

00:05:33.046 --> 00:05:35.607
screen. You will need the three words when

00:05:35.607 --> 00:05:38.525
that checklist asks what a grid is. A

00:05:38.525 --> 00:05:41.097
paper or demo account is a fence around

00:05:41.097 --> 00:05:43.661
practice. Inside the fence you can see

00:05:43.661 --> 00:05:46.133
fields and buttons. You still do not send

00:05:46.133 --> 00:05:49.362
an order in this course. If you keep one

00:05:49.362 --> 00:05:51.731
sentence, keep this: range, levels, and

00:05:51.731 --> 00:05:54.578
stop, drawn before any click. Bouncing

00:05:54.578 --> 00:05:56.792
inside the band is what a grid is built

00:05:56.792 --> 00:05:59.529
for. The exit from the band is the failure

00:05:59.529 --> 00:06:02.979
picture. A grid bot places waiting buys

00:06:02.979 --> 00:06:05.354
below the price and waiting sells above

00:06:05.354 --> 00:06:09.149
it. This 2023 path stayed between the

00:06:09.149 --> 00:06:11.808
bottom line and the top line, with six

00:06:11.808 --> 00:06:15.740
gaps of about 900 between the lines. The

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:17.853
stop rule says what you will do if the

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:20.957
price leaves and does not come back. Next

00:06:20.957 --> 00:06:23.585
lesson: What you are going to need. Bring

00:06:23.585 --> 00:06:25.643
your notes: the top and bottom of the

00:06:25.532 --> 00:06:27.867
band, the gaps between the lines, and your

00:06:27.747 --> 00:06:30.643
stop rule. Leave every figure marked

00:06:30.643 --> 00:06:33.008
Example. No order is sent between lessons.

